Z||000000||AkursedX||09-25-2000||10:09 PM||||Ok, well I'm in my school parking lot on my way back to my car, and I see a pretty funny sight.  <BR>Well it's not exactly a "Ricer"  but it was about a 1996 Pontiac Bonneville.  It was black with tinted windows, lowered, chrome exhaust tip, and these HUGE UGLY chrome rims!!  Well this in itself is pretty common and not worth a story.  But as I look closer, I take a look at the tires.  They were some sort of Pierelli's, but I notice something odd about the tread.  It appears that all of his tires are on BACKWARDS!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>How stupid can some people be??  It must be fun hydroplaning everywhere, because the treads would actually bring more water under the tire with them on backwards.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||10
